#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:4164
#, no-c-format
msgid "Installation"
msgstr "Installacion"

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:4167
#, no-c-format
msgid "How to Obtain &kalarm;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: sect1
#: index.docbook:4167
#, no-c-format
msgid "&install.intro.documentation;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4171
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kalarm; is available for &kde; 2 and as a standalone package for &kde; 3 "
"from <ulink url=\"http://www.astrojar.org.uk/kalarm\">http://www.astrojar."
"org.uk/kalarm</ulink>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:4178
#, no-c-format
msgid "Requirements"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4180
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kalarm; requires the standard &kde; libraries to be installed (the "
"<filename>kdelibs</filename> package). To compile from source, you also need "
"the &Qt; and <filename>kdelibs</filename> development packages. The X11 "
"development package, if present, is used to improve &kalarm;'s ability to "
"function under &kde; without a system tray."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4187
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The following optional packages enhance &kalarm; at runtime if they are "
"installed:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4191
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kmix; (from kdemultimedia package): if installed, it allows &kalarm; to set "
"the absolute sound volume when playing audio files."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4196
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<application>KTTSD</application> (from kdeaccessibility package): if "
"installed and configured, together with a compatible speech synthesizer "
"package, it allows &kalarm; to speak alarm messages when they are displayed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4203
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kalarm; uses about 12 Mb of memory to run, but this may vary depending on "
"your platform and configuration."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4206
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can find a list of changes in the <filename>ChangeLog</filename> file, "
"or at <ulink url=\"http://www.astrojar.org.uk/kalarm\">http://www.astrojar."
"org.uk/kalarm</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:4212
#, no-c-format
msgid "Compilation and Installation"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4214
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you cannot obtain a suitable precompiled binary package, you need to "
"compile &kalarm; yourself from source files. Get the source package file "
"<filename>kdepim-x.x.tar.bz2</filename> or <filename>kalarm-x.x.tar.bz2</"
"filename> (or similar), depending on whether you want to install &package; "
"or just &kalarm;. Unpack it in a new folder using a command similar to "
"<userinput><command>tar</command> <option>xvfj <replaceable>package.tar.bz2</"
"replaceable></option></userinput>, and change to the folder which has been "
"created."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: sect1
#: index.docbook:4222
#, no-c-format
msgid "&install.compile.documentation;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4226
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have more than one version of &kde; installed (e.g. &kde; 2 and &kde; "
"3), this may possibly install &kalarm; into the wrong &kde; folder. If "
"necessary, you can give the &kde; folder as a parameter to "
"<userinput><command>./configure</command></userinput> . For example, if your "
"&kde; is installed in <filename>/opt/kde2</filename>:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: index.docbook:4233
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>./configure</command> --prefix=<replaceable>/opt/kde2</replaceable>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4236
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you install &kalarm; into a folder different from where &kde; is "
"installed, it will not run correctly unless you make its location known to "
"&kde;. To do this, you must prefix the <envar>KDEDIRS</envar> environment "
"variable with &kalarm;'s location, each time before you start &kde;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4242
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For example, if &kde; is installed in <literal>/opt/kde</literal>, "
"<envar>KDEDIRS</envar> might normally be set to <literal>/etc/opt/kde:/opt/"
"kde</literal>. If you install &kalarm; into <literal>/usr/local</literal>, "
"you would need to set <envar>KDEDIRS</envar> to <literal>/usr/local:/etc/opt/"
"kde:/opt/kde</literal> before starting &kde;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4250
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The standalone version of &kalarm; has a special configuration option which "
"allows you to select which languages documentation is to be installed for by "
"specifying a language code, or a list of language codes, as a parameter to "
"<command>./configure</command>. By default, documentation in all available "
"languages is installed. A list of documentation languages included in the "
"package, together with their codes, is in the <filename>DOC-LANGUAGES</"
"filename> file. For example, to install only French and British English "
"documentation:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: index.docbook:4259
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>./configure</command> --enable-doc-language=<replaceable>\"fr en_GB"
"\"</replaceable>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4261
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Note that this option has no effect on which user interface translations are "
"installed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:4267
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuration"
msgstr "Configuracion"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4269
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"No special configuration is required to set up &kalarm; to run on the &kde; "
"desktop. Once you have run &kalarm; for the first time, it will start every "
"time you log in, in order to monitor scheduled alarms."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4274
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To run &kalarm; on a non-&kde; desktop, the main requirement is to ensure "
"that &kalarm; is run automatically whenever you log in. More detailed "
"instructions are contained in the <filename>INSTALL</filename> file which is "
"distributed with &kalarm;."
msgstr ""
